With the establishment of [[:en:State Shinto|State Shinto]], the shrine was designated as a {{nihongo|prefectural shrine|県社|1=Prefectural Shrine|qid=Q90139226}}{{efn|Ken-sha|lt=Ken-sha|1=Modern_system_of_ranked_Shinto_shrines#Metropolitan_and_Prefectural_Shrines||}}. In 1931, the ''[[Honden]]'' of the shrine, dating from the [[:en:Muromachi period|Muromachi period]], was designated a National [[:en:Important Cultural Property (Japan)|Important Cultural Property]].
The shrine is located a 15-minute walk from [[:en:Etchū-Kokubu Station|Etchū-Kokubu Station]] on the [[:en:West Japan Railway Company|West Japan Railway Company]] [[:en:Himi Line|Himi Line]].<ref name="Okada">{{cite book |last1=Okada |first1=Shoji |title=Taiyō no chizuchō 24 zenkoku `Ichinomiya' meguri |date=2014 |publisher=Heibonsha |isbn=4582945619 |language=Japanese}}</ref>
